Hello,

while upgrading the kernel on my amilo laptop
(slackware 12.1, gcc-4.2.3), and after ditching 2.6.25.8 because of
many build warnings about  mismatched sections and discarding
of qualifiers when passing arguments to functions,
I tried building 2.6.26-rc7, and even though everything went
much better, some warnings still remain:

mm/slab.c: In function 'kfree':
mm/slab.c:3794: warning: passing argument 2 of '__cache_free' discards qualifier
s from pointer target type

fs/cifs/dir.c: In function 'cifs_ci_compare':
fs/cifs/dir.c:613: warning: passing argument 1 of '__constant_memcpy' discards q
ualifiers from pointer target type
fs/cifs/dir.c:613: warning: passing argument 1 of '__memcpy' discards qualifiers
 from pointer target type

fs/partitions/check.c: In function 'add_partition':
fs/partitions/check.c:381: warning: ignoring return value of 'device_add', decla
red with attribute warn_unused_result

block/genhd.c: In function 'add_disk':
block/genhd.c:195: warning: ignoring return value of 'sysfs_create_link', declar
ed with attribute warn_unused_result

include/asm/io_32.h: In function 'memcpy_fromio':
include/asm/io_32.h:210: warning: passing argument 2 of '__memcpy'
discards qualifiers from pointer target type

drivers/video/aty/radeon_base.c: In function 'radeonfb_pci_register':
drivers/video/aty/radeon_base.c:2343: warning: ignoring return value
of 'sysfs_create_bin_file', declared with attribute warn_unused_result
drivers/video/aty/radeon_base.c:2345: warning: ignoring return value
of 'sysfs_create_bin_file', declared with attribute warn_unused_result

